r with and i  trust that this  will be informative for people in other  regions as well but do your research for  your region and if you're wondering well  how shall i do this how shall i find  this information for my country  i created a course on salary  negotiations together with a good friend  of mine who is also former consultant i  will link this course below in the video  description  and there's also full module on the  topic of salary research such as this  will contain some interesting insights  last but not least i will now talk about  base salary so the base salaries that  you would pretty much get  fixed independent of your performance on  top of that most firms have also bonus  that they're offered to you and this is  usually up to 20  or so so if you're rated in the highest  performance category  this is what you can expect of course  most people will not get the highest  rating inside a performance rating which  is about average or slightly above  average  you can expect to get a bonus which will  roughly be 10  of your base salary so this is what you  should then add on top  to the numbers that i will mention to  you and then of course if you look at  the full compensation package  most firms also offer something like a  company car that you will get even as a  junior consultant and then there are  other benefits like insurances or  additional travel allowances that will  be provided to you  which you should add on top of this base  salary that we will be discussing right  now so let's get into it and discuss the  individual roads in detail  and while i will now also provide a  little characterization of the roads if  you really no idea  how this works what the roads the  responsibilities of these different  positions exactly are  i created a full video on that was  called how a career in consulting looks  like  and i will link it somewhere above here  so check this out if this is all new to  you and you really want to understand a  bit better  how the whole career path in consulting  looks like so the first role i want to  talk about is the business analyst role  and how exactly these  roads are called changes a bit firm by  firm they all have their own terminology  then the end is all the same right and  the business analyst role is the role  that you will have  fresh out of university if you leave a  university with a bachelor or master  degree  you just start out in consulting this is  the role that you will have of course  in this role you will usually crunch the  numbers conduct  interviews with clients create slight  decks so this is really the role where  you learn the ropes of the trait and for  this role in a country like germany you  can expect a salary  of roughly 70 000 euro per year for a  master level graduate which is of course  a very decent starting salary for a new  graduate you will have this business  analyst role for about two years  and after two years most of these tier  one firms offer something which is very  unique and this is the so-called  leaf program and here again how exactly  it's called difference a bit company by  company but what essentially it boils  down to is that the company will give  you the opportunity  to leave work again and to spend some  time to conduct a phd  or mba or often also social leave  year if you want to volunteer for a  social organization  and this time which usually takes two to  three years will be heavily  subsidized by your employer so for  instance if you do an mba the company  usually will sponsor a significant  portion of the tuition of your mba and  they will pay you money on top  often also up to a full salary just to  cover your living expenses in this time  and here even within the t1 firms there  can be significant differences in how  exactly this program  is set up how attractive it is and what  i learned now from talking to other  friends probably the mckinsey one is  arguably the most attractive then  followed by the boston consulting  followed by the bane and here also what  i want you to understand is that many of  these smaller tier 2 firms offer  programs like this  as well but then if you look into them  often they're not as attractive or maybe  they are saying yes you can do that but  in the end it turns out that only if  you're ranked  as one of the top top performers you  will really be offered to do this and  then the big majority of consultants in  the end will not have this opportunity  so i'd argue that this is really  something that on top of the regular  salary differences really sets apart  these p1 firms from these other firms  and you really should take this into  account when you compare the total  compensation package  in the first years of your time in  consulting because the value of the  compensation package that you get in  this leave  program can easily be in the six digits  so really have a look at this closely  before you ask yourself what company you  want to join after all then after the  leave usually you enter an  associate type of position this is also  the position that you will directly be  able to join  if you join consulting with an mba or  with a phd  in terms of the contents of your job  this is pretty much just an extension of  what you were doing  as a business analyst with the only  difference that now more is expected  from you so you will be now expected to  lead  larger parts of the project you will be  expected now to do things standalone  with very little guidance from your  project lead  just the workload the expectations the  responsibilities  you have will just increase will expand  compared to these other roads  and as an associate you can expect to  earn around 110  000 euro in germany again with  differences company by company so this  is indeed a significant salary increase  to the road that you had earlier then  this associate role is again something  that you will often do for about two  years or so  and then you advance and the project  lead role this is now the role where you  will be responsible for consulting teams  working on the ground and the client a  typical consulting team is the project  lead plus  one to four consultants so total team of  two to five consultants and then on top  of course you also have the junior  partners partners senior partners who  come on top will provide some guidance  and join you occasionally so as a  project lead you can expect to earn 140  to 150  000 euro base salary every year and then  at the project lead level  with many firms also the bonuses start  to increase so maybe you might have the  potential to earning up to  30 or even more bonus on top of your  base salary instead of maybe only 20  which was rather the norm for the lower  levels so this is now the first level  where also the compensation will vary  more significantly based on your  performance that you will bring to the  table in your job then after the project  lead role most firms distinguish  different levels of partner roads so  often it starts with a junior partner  level  which you will have for another two  years or so until then you can get  elected  partner of the firm this is now this  real full partner role which is often  the aspiration  of many many people then still want to  continue their career in consulting and  then after four to five years or so in  your partner role you can become a  senior partner which is then in terms of  job title  the highest level that you can reach so  when we discuss the salaries of these  different partner levels here it's  important to understand that these  salary structures are getting much more  complex so besides the base salary of  there's a component which is linked to  the performance of the company over roy  so how good is the  company doing overall that you're  working for this will affect your salary  and then also your performance element  so the bonus that you will get paid on  top of that  this will now pay an increasingly  important role of your overall  compensation but that being said as a  junior partner you can then expect to  earn  something about 200 to 250 000 euro  and then once you're really getting  elected a full partner this will usually  be above 300 000 euro in salary this  salary will then increase over time  again heavily also influenced by your  performance once you're a senior partner  this can then be rather around 600 to  800  000 euro and indeed the best earning  best performing senior partners  can earn in the millions so we'll earn  several million euro every year  of course while these figures sound very  high it's also important to understand  that it's not necessarily  easy to become partner there's a sole  concept an idea of the upper out  principle  if you never heard about that i willing  the video above here that i did on this  topic so in a nutshell  people will get filtered out many people  will get asked to leave the firm at some  point in their career only the very best  of course will have the opportunity to  become partner and then earn salaries in  these dimensions so now i'd be  interested to hear from you  is this surprising to you does this meet  your experiences and expectations  do you think these salaries are  extremely high or maybe not even that  high if you consider all the work that  goes into such a career  let me know your views in the comments  and as you know i will do my very best  to answer every single comment that you  write so if you took any value out of  this video at all  please hit the like button for the  youtube algorithm and also subscribe to  the channel and especially also turn on  the notification bell to stay up to date  on all my content if you want to see  even more from me also follow me on my  instagram my handle is from learning and  now as  always i also want to say thank you to  all the members of the channel you're  really making a difference a big  contribution to the work to the course  of this channel and if you are  interested in becoming a member as well  just click on the join button next to  the subscribe button to see how you can  support and also earn some member only  perks to all the rest of you  thank you for watching until the very  end i'm releasing new videos every  single  saturday and especially also next  saturday i have a very interesting video  planned for you so stay tuned  good weekend to all of you talk to you  next saturday this is heine from from  learning  bye-bye

